[{:db/id "q-119054/selection/7ca428b612ce8f05b43cde3d79925b10ef8c05d532c9673c5a2a27095a6d7626" :answer/id #uuid "5d7149ac-2bbd-5157-b847-7e20a49ac8d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=-kM,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054/selection/88adf12396fe0144bd4394dc6dc230b082a288f931b281e4f9915dcef5a8b1cf" :answer/id #uuid "204adecc-48ac-589a-a2c4-c45b2bb9c566" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=kM,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054/selection/84e0a55c5d477491f8e92ee174b50965bf94df8f4897117e0a139caae1709ece" :answer/id #uuid "a240a70d-4182-51c1-9562-8bd784e6db5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{M},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054/selection/c0a209b91bcfcd6b0f2c4419021dab8572405ccdeccb8f3f87f8a99399ee4f1f" :answer/id #uuid "5bf19db2-ca38-5089-b7d8-8b06876fecbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=k+M,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054/selection/e5117a6ff58934d8ec12f63f8dd2b100641c5cb4aea6c233df1aecb2eaab0335" :answer/id #uuid "d6aadcb2-900d-53bc-b91a-9e4af7e70d99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}\\text{M}}{\\text{d}t}=-k{M}^{2},\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c61bbc42-877d-5f75-b824-673922e2d663" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119054/selection/88adf12396fe0144bd4394dc6dc230b082a288f931b281e4f9915dcef5a8b1cf" :answer-field/choices ["q-119054/selection/7ca428b612ce8f05b43cde3d79925b10ef8c05d532c9673c5a2a27095a6d7626" "q-119054/selection/88adf12396fe0144bd4394dc6dc230b082a288f931b281e4f9915dcef5a8b1cf" "q-119054/selection/84e0a55c5d477491f8e92ee174b50965bf94df8f4897117e0a139caae1709ece" "q-119054/selection/c0a209b91bcfcd6b0f2c4419021dab8572405ccdeccb8f3f87f8a99399ee4f1f" "q-119054/selection/e5117a6ff58934d8ec12f63f8dd2b100641c5cb4aea6c233df1aecb2eaab0335"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119054" :question/id #uuid "fa32ad2d-05af-5067-9118-2c0c283b8d2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-119054" :question/problem "The amount of money $M(t)$ in a saving account increases at a rate that is proportional to the amount of money currently in the account. What differential equation describes the rate of change in the amount of money in the saving account $M,$ at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **amount of money** $M(t)$ in a saving account **increases** at a **rate** that is **proportional** to the **amount of money** currently in the saving account.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *amount of money* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *amount of money.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}∝M.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the amount of money *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=kM.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119054/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255dee12-5f44-536b-b679-5a894843395d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection/8c516ba3711f978789a06d975d6cd3bfcd6e41bf7a3e5739aec8cc512374c5e5" :answer/id #uuid "f2c509b0-e6da-5199-994a-ce81c59fc86d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-k{M}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection/fe6a703b31691df41dccba30307cd9c1487f30f6d623824b5642291c0b253a72" :answer/id #uuid "22c53dcf-4d03-528b-b10d-afdce686e0a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{M}^{2}},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection/2ba7e1a1386a20a8ccc7f23cbf07344757fe8a66ca2c914497851ecb98dbde6b" :answer/id #uuid "9040d995-4b91-5e52-95f2-d5cb882a3dd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=k{M}^{2},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection/ec2796424ac0e30150d29f93ba9895c7f962118caf70b59195b94dc40dbe87ed" :answer/id #uuid "a0b2ef34-4c74-5b5f-b815-305fd9653851" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-k\\sqrt{M},\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection/bb83dcc8996573c9948f3ed8e25cb5322742598016ea52f67780c3b003d351c5" :answer/id #uuid "82327f25-b37f-5b73-a9c3-1e5026b7b754" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-kM,\\,\\,k>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8f1b0ad4-b3f0-58ba-847e-112cee74785f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143038/selection/8c516ba3711f978789a06d975d6cd3bfcd6e41bf7a3e5739aec8cc512374c5e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-143038/selection/8c516ba3711f978789a06d975d6cd3bfcd6e41bf7a3e5739aec8cc512374c5e5" "q-143038/selection/fe6a703b31691df41dccba30307cd9c1487f30f6d623824b5642291c0b253a72" "q-143038/selection/2ba7e1a1386a20a8ccc7f23cbf07344757fe8a66ca2c914497851ecb98dbde6b" "q-143038/selection/ec2796424ac0e30150d29f93ba9895c7f962118caf70b59195b94dc40dbe87ed" "q-143038/selection/bb83dcc8996573c9948f3ed8e25cb5322742598016ea52f67780c3b003d351c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143038" :question/id #uuid "b29e13ab-6240-5953-8f63-4daf76f87654" :question/math-academy-id "q-143038" :question/problem "During a chemical reaction, the mass $M$ of a particular substance decreases with time. The rate of change of the substance's mass is proportional to the square of the mass. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the substance's mass at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*During a chemical reaction, the **mass** $M$ of a particular substance  **decreases** with time. The **rate** of change of the substance's mass is **proportional** to the **square of the mass**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *mass* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *mass squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}∝{M}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the mass *decreases* with time, our derivative should be *negative*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}M}{\\text{d}t}=-k{M}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "344f1838-a027-5fd5-82da-17e9b4fcac2b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-143076"] :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume $V$ of a balloon** being inflated **increases** at a rate that's **inversely proportional** to the **square of the volume**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *inversely proportional to* the *square of volume.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝\\frac{1}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the volume *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{k}{{V}^{2}}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
